# CH14 build outputs.
#
# Scoped to this chapter rather than added to the repository root, so CH14 is
# self-sufficient and nothing here changes what any other chapter sees.
#
# Nothing generated is tracked, which matches the rest of the repository --
# `git ls-files` finds no .bit, .hwh or .xsa anywhere in it. Both builds are
# reproducible from what IS tracked:
#
#   vivado -mode batch -source project_sysmon_lcd/build.tcl   # .bit .hwh .xsa
#   vitis  -s sw_mb/build_app.py                              # .elf

# The Vivado project the new design is built in, and the artifacts it exports.
/project_sysmon_lcd/vivado/
/project_sysmon_lcd/out/

# The Vitis workspace (platform, BSP, application) and the ELF it produces.
/sw_mb/workspace/
/sw_mb/out/

# The host-native unit test binaries.
/sw_mb/build/

# The Vivado project of the design CH14 originally shipped. build/bd/hw.tcl is
# its SOURCE and is tracked -- project_sysmon_lcd/build.tcl sources that file
# to get the block design and the PS configuration, so without it the new
# design cannot be rebuilt. Everything else under build/ is output.
/build/*
!/build/bd/
!/build/xdc/

# Tool droppings, at every level.
*.jou
*.log
*.str
.Xil/
hs_err_pid*.log
__pycache__/

# Vivado project trees left by the other language directories.
*.cache/
*.gen/
*.hw/
*.ip_user_files/
*.runs/
*.sim/
*.srcs/
*.xpr
*.xsa
